Rejected—no generator is shipped.

The [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.10238) provides polynomial-time algorithms for the generatable near-half independent-set regime; its hardness results are worst-case and do not justify a planted distribution.

The tested Track B construction failed because:

- The oracle harness returned `too_easy` after all three escalations.
- The final rung was solved by 2/3 genuine oracle attempts.
- A construction-aware affine-frame attack recovered valid witnesses on 80/80 tests.
- The reference algorithm costs at most 616,296 GF(2) operations, while the exposed shortcut takes at most 263 XORs.

Full evidence is in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2405.10238/REJECTED.md) and [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2405.10238/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl). The [experimental module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2405.10238/gen_2405_10238.py) is retained and now correctly reports G6 failure. Shipping README, self-test report, and G9 transcripts were intentionally not created because STEP 4 required stopping.
